  "summary": [
    "Early-year data show about 606 Mediterranean deaths by late February 2026, implying a high near-term toll path but not certainty about hitting 900 by end of March.",
    "To reach 900 by April, March would need roughly 294 deaths; continuing the February pace or worse remains plausible but not assured.",
    "Countervailing factors include policy and deterrence measures that could reduce crossings, and SAR capacity improvements that could lower fatalities; data revisions could push counts upward if backlog gets cleared.",
    "Overall, the forecast tilts moderately downward from the initial anchor, reflecting mixed near-term dynamics and substantial uncertainty."
  ],
  "confidence": "medium",
  "narrative": "Starting from a high early-year signal (606 deaths by late Feb 2026), a mix of factors suggests the March total is plausible but uncertain and likely below the starting anchor of 0.75 probability. The calibrated 0.62 probability reflects competing forces: some upward pressures from data revisions, but meaningful downward pressures from policy responses and rescue improvements.",
  "justification": {
    "anchor": {
      "probability": 0.75,
      "basis": "Reference class is IOM Missing Migrants Project Mediterranean route deaths; the anchor uses the observed early-year pace (around 606 deaths by late February 2026) as a short-term baseline, which implies a higher likelihood of a rapid total if March remains deadly."
    },
    "factor_updates": [
      {
        "factor": "Pace of early-year fatalities persisting into March",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Continuing to hit 294+ deaths in March to reach 900 by end of March is a steep continuation of the February pace; if March slows, the probability declines."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Data reporting lags and potential revisions to counts",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Backlogs and late-month revisions can push March totals upward, partially offsetting downward pressure from other factors."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Policy crackdown and reduced search-and-rescue capacity",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Stricter controls and signaling of deterrence may push some crossings toward riskier routes or reduce rescues, potentially increasing fatalities and the probability of hitting 900."
      },
      {
        "factor": "SAR capacity improvements",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Expanded rescue capacity and safer pathways could reduce deaths, lowering the near-term risk of reaching 900."
      },
      {
        "factor": "March weather volatility and month-to-month variability",
        "direction": "neutral",
        "magnitude": "weak",
        "rationale": "Uncertain weather conditions could either raise or lower fatalities, with no clear directional bias."
      }
    ],
    "synthesis_rationale": "Starting from a high anchor (0.75) based on early-year data, the mix of downward (pace persistence, SAR improvements) and upward (data revisions, policy-driven risks) updates yields a net tilt toward lower probability than the anchor. The calibrated probability of 0.62 reflects substantial near-term uncertainty, with a range that accommodates potential upward revisions but also the possibility that March does not sustain the February surge."
  }
